The ruck started off with a 2 mile shared ruck carry over hill and over dale with 3- 60# and one 105# sandbags in play.  Those bags are easy until you're trying to go up OR down a hill!

After bags were stashed, we headed into the depths of the Anthills trails, going up, down, and around all the while keeping head on a swivel for roots, holes, blind drop offs and the occasional spider web.

At the 4 mile mark we stopped to top off water and a few exercises.

-1 min low plank w ruck 
- ruck squats
- ruck swings
- overhead ruck flutter kicks

Back on the move we pushed the next three miles before jumping to the "improved" asphalt trail, riddled with cracking/shifting sections of trail in the dark.  At mile 11-12 the PAX decided to do a ruck wolf trot to gain some time/distance. 

The last 2 miles we pushed hard at a good clip to wrap up this little adventure.  

It was a great time with some great HIMs that honored me by helping me entertain the fruition of this CSAUP.  Special thanks to 
@Zelda for the awesome event patches and for the continued prods to get this organized.

